  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200, especially with transformer aggregation, reaching about 0.653 validation accuracy. In contrast, image evidence is sparse and weak: image-only ResNet50 single-profile performs poorly at about 0.208 accuracy. config_013 tests whether a stronger ImageNet ViT-L image encoder can make the image modality useful in the simplest image-only setting, isolating image representation from RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion choices. This is the best next experiment because it reduces the key uncertainty of whether image features are worth using before investing in more complex multimodal configurations, while still potentially identifying a strong image-only baseline."
}

